  "raw": " substance that caused her to lose consciousness\n\nOkay you didn't murder her.\n\nAt the end of the day, if a woman runs a bath for you - even if it's for her own comfort and welfare - you think nothing of it.\n\nBut tell her you want one for yourself and she will think you're a complete and utter weirdo.\n\nThat's just what happened to Julia Knight, an A cooker, on the night of October 20, 2014, at Horton Hospital in Banbury.\n\nAnd the patient nurse said she provided the 9-volt battery and, rather to her horror, claimed she then administered it.\n\nThe Crown Prosecution Service, however, are arguing that Knight, 56, of Moston Lane, Oadby, Mansfield, should have instead provided earlier treatment when the standard psychiatric procedure was in place.\n\nShe pleaded guilty at Oxford Crown Court in June 2015 to administering a substance that caused the patient to lose consciousness.",
  "serialized": "substance that caused her to lose consciousness Okay you didn't murder her. At the end of the day, if a woman runs a bath for you - even if it's for her own comfort and welfare - you think nothing of it. But tell her you want one for yourself and she will think you're a complete and utter weirdo. That's just what happened to Julia Knight, an A cooker, on the night of October 20, 2014, at Horton Hospital in Banbury. And the patient nurse said she provided the 9-volt battery and, rather to her horror, claimed she then administered it. The Crown Prosecution Service, however, are arguing that Knight, 56, of Moston Lane, Oadby, Mansfield, should have instead provided earlier treatment when the standard psychiatric procedure was in place. She pleaded guilty at Oxford Crown Court in June 2015 to administering a substance that caused the patient to lose consciousness.",
